# Adding an agent host or MCP client

Ship **constants + developer config + docs + public landing/hub wiring** in the same change. Do not defer docs or Access-panel snippets.

Two product surfaces share the `/agents` hub but use **different** content trees:

| Kind | Examples | Landing seed | Docs section | Developer Access |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| **Agent host** | OpenClaw, Hermes, Grok Bot | `web/src/lib/content/constants/agents/{slug}.ts` | `web/src/content/docs/agent-setup-guides/` | openquok-core / CLI skill (not `MCP_CLIENTS`) |
| **MCP client** | Cursor, ChatGPT, Warp | `web/src/lib/content/constants/mcps/{slug}.ts` | `web/src/content/docs/mcp-setup-guides/` | `getMcpClientConfig` + `MCP_CLIENTS` |

Follow **source-project-neutrality** and **company-brand-icons**. Reference MCP client: **`chatgpt.ts`**, **`claude-cowork.ts`**, **`warp.ts`**. Reference agent host: **`openclaw.ts`**, **`hermes.ts`**, **`grok-bot.ts`**.

**Do not edit `backend/supabase/db/**`** for agent launches (no listing-tag seeds, no blog seeds, no migration re-aggregate). Catalog tags and launch blog posts go in through secret-admin UI — see **C. CMS (blog + listing tag)** below.

---

## Identifier contract

Use one **lowercase kebab-case** slug everywhere:

- Seed `slug` / `agentId`
- Filename under `mcps/` or `agents/`
- Docs page: `mcp-setup-guides/{slug}.md` or `agent-setup-guides/{slug}.md`
- `MCP_CLIENT_DOCS_SLUG` value (MCP clients only)
- Public URL: `/agents/{slug}` (and `/agents/{slug}/{channelSlug}` when channel SEO applies)

`mcpClient` label (MCP clients) must be a member of `MCP_CLIENTS` in `getMcpClientConfig.ts` — exact string match.

### Hero title gradient highlights

Landing heroes (`heroTitle` is usually `Schedule social media from {label} then you approve`) pick up gradient styling via `LANDING_HERO_TITLE_HIGHLIGHT_WORDS` in **`web/src/lib/ui/templates/landing-page/landingHeroTheme.ts`**.

Append the **product name as it appears in `heroTitle`** (seed `label` / `agentLabel`). Examples: `'openclaw'`, `'hermes'`, `'Grok Bot'`. Matching is case-insensitive; multi-word labels need the full phrase (e.g. `'Grok Bot'`, not `'grok'`).

Applies to agent-host and MCP landing pages, the `/agents` hub, and any surface that passes `landingHeroTheme` into `HeroMain`.

