## B. Adding an agent host (e.g. OpenClaw)

### 1. Branded icon

Same as MCP clients — `branded-icons.ts`.

### 2. Agent landing seed

**`web/src/lib/content/constants/agents/{slug}.ts`** + register in **`agents/index.ts`** (and hub copy in `hub.ts` / shared FAQs when needed).

Add host-specific **`skillInstallOptions`** in **`openquokCliCommandReference.ts`** when install differs from OpenClaw (Hermes CLI, Grok Bot workspace + Plugins, etc.).

### 3. Messaging / workflow mocks (agent hosts)

Do **not** let new hosts fall through to OpenClaw Telegram/WhatsApp in **`PublicAgentLandingPage.svelte`**. Either reuse Hermes/OpenClaw channel data or add **`web/src/data/{slug}-messaging-channels.ts`** and branch in the landing page map.

| File | Agent-host mocks |
| --- | --- |
| `safariMock.types.ts` + `SafariMockContent.svelte` | `{slug}-docs-overview` + `*DocsOverviewMock.svelte` |
| `terminalMock.types.ts` + `TerminalCommandMockContent.svelte` | `openquok-skill-install-{slug}` when install is terminal-driven |

Telegram-first hosts (OpenClaw, Hermes): `iphone-15-pro` + `agent-chat-schedule`. Desktop-first hosts (Grok Bot): `desktop` workflow mocks.

Wire onboarding: **`OnboardingAgentConnectStep.svelte`** tab + official docs link; **`OnboardingAgentCliStep.svelte`** docs href; **`account/+page.svelte`** landing + guide shortcut cards.

### 4. Docs

**`web/src/content/docs/agent-setup-guides/{slug}.md`** + **`agent-setup-guides/index.md`** `LinkCard`. Cross-link CLI auth / openquok-core as appropriate. Mention the host in **`hub.ts`**, **`getting-started-for-cli/index.md`**, **`mcp-setup-guides/index.md`** (agent-hosts sentence), **`other-skills/index.md`**, **`publicSkillBuilderFaqConfig.ts`**, and **`publicFaqConfig.ts`** when OpenClaw/Hermes are named.

### 5. Channel SEO (when shipping per-channel agent pages)

Follow patterns under `web/src/lib/content/constants/agents/channels/` and **add-social-provider-integration** for `/agents/{agentSlug}/{channelSlug}`. Append slug to **`PUBLIC_AGENT_CHANNEL_HOST_SLUGS`** in `agents/channels/index.ts`.

### 6. Skills / CLI

Update `agent/skills/openquok-core/` (`SKILL.md` metadata JSON for the host when discovery differs) and related docs under `getting-started-for-cli` / `cli-usages` only when the host’s install path changes.

### Grok Bot specifics (`grok-bot`)

- **Not** an MCP client — no `mcps/grok-bot.ts`, no `MCP_CLIENTS`, no `mcp-setup-guides/grok-bot.md`.
- Cloud computer + desktop/iOS chat; skill via **`/workspace/openquok-core/SKILL.md`** and **Settings → Plugins** (or `/` in chat).
- Reference implementation: **`grok-bot.ts`**, **`grok-bot-messaging-channels.ts`**, **`GROK_BOT_SKILL_INSTALL_OPTIONS`**.

### Agent host PR checklist

- [ ] Icon + agent seed registered; hub lists the host
- [ ] `landingHeroTheme.ts` — `LANDING_HERO_TITLE_HIGHLIGHT_WORDS` includes the host label
- [ ] `skillInstallOptions` + messaging channels (no OpenClaw fallback on landing)
- [ ] Safari/terminal mock ids + onboarding + account shortcuts
- [ ] `agent-setup-guides/{slug}.md` + index card + cross-mentions in hub/CLI/FAQ copy
- [ ] Channel SEO in `agents/channels/` if `/agents/{slug}/{channel}` is in scope
- [ ] **CMS:** listing tag + launch blog via secret-admin (see **C**); no `backend/supabase/db` edits
- [ ] Smoke `/agents/{slug}` and docs page

